   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Dynamic Text\n\nWord-to-word morph where letters are physical: shared letters glide to their new spot on a spring arc, others fall away, new ones drop in and land with a squash.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 7.2 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A headline word should change into another while keeping the letters they share, so the change reads as one object transforming.\n- A counter or a short list of words (Create, Iterate, Repeat, Ship) needs a physical, tactile swap.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The two words share almost no letters and a plain swap is enough: use slide-swap or per-word-crossfade.\n- A whole sentence changes: use kinetic-morph-text.\n\nVariables:\n- texts (string): Words, default \"Create|Iterate|Repeat|Ship\"\n- interval (number, 0.8-4): Interval, default 1.8\n- font_size (number, 24-260): Font size, default 120\n- color (color): Color, default \"#18181b\"\n- font_weight (enum): Font weight, default \"600\"\n\nSource: https://github.com/kokonut-labs/kokonutui. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Dynamic Text\n\n  Morphing text where letters are physical objects: the first word's letters drop in and land with a squash; when the word changes, shared letters travel to their new place on a spring arc, leaving letters tip and fall off the baseline, new letters drop in, and digits roll like a counter.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/kokonut-labs/kokonutui/blob/4d497b7b03f02ffd07225e638c0b9ace3f892dbb/components/kokonutui/dynamic-text.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2025 kokonutUI\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"dynamic-text\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"7.2\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"texts\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Words\", \"description\": \"Words separated by |. The text morphs from each one to the next. Digits roll like a counter.\", \"default\": \"Create|Iterate|Repeat|Ship\"},\n    {\"id\": \"interval\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Interval\", \"description\": \"Seconds each word holds before the morph to the next.\", \"default\": 1.8, \"min\": 0.8, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.1, \"unit\": \"s\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Maximum text size in pixels. Wide words shrink to fit the frame.\", \"default\": 120, \"min\": 24, \"max\": 260, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Color\", \"description\": \"Text color.\", \"default\": \"#18181b\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_weight\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font weight\", \"description\": \"Weight of the text.\", \"default\": \"600\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"500\", \"label\": \"Medium\"}, {\"value\": \"600\", \"label\": \"Semibold\"}, {\"value\": \"700\", \"label\": \"Bold\"}]}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Dynamic Text</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@500;600;700&amp;display=block\" />\n      <style>\n        #root { position: absolute; inset: 0; overflow: hidden; container-type: size; pointer-events: none; }\n        #root { font-family: var(--font-display, Geist, system-ui, sans-serif); color: var(--dt-color, #18181b); }\n        .dt-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n        .dt-row { position: relative; line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -0.03em; white-space: pre; height: 1.15em; }\n        .dt-glyph { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; transform-origin: 50% 100%; opacity: 0; white-space: pre; }\n        .dt-measure { position: absolute; left: -9999px; top: 0; visibility: hidden; white-space: pre; line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -0.03em; }\n        .dt-measure span { display: inline-block; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"dynamic-text\" data-duration=\"7.2\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"dt-clip\" class=\"dt-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"7.2\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div id=\"dt-row\" class=\"dt-row\" role=\"img\"></div>\n        </div>\n        <div id=\"dt-measure\" class=\"dt-measure\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars = window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables() : {};\n            function num(v, f, a, b) { var x = Number(v); return Number.isFinite(x) ? Math.min(b, Math.max(a, x)) : f; }\n            function str(v, f) { return typeof v === \"string\" && v.trim() ? v : f; }\n            function col(v, f) { return typeof v === \"string\" && v ? v : f; }\n            function mulberry32(a) { return function () { a |= 0; a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0; var t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a); t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t; return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; }; }\n            function clamp01(x) { return x < 0 ? 0 : x > 1 ? 1 : x; }\n\n\n            var row = document.getElementById(\"dt-row\");\n            var measure = document.getElementById(\"dt-measure\");\n            var words = str(vars.texts, \"Create|Iterate|Repeat|Ship\").split(\"|\").map(function (s) { return s.trim(); }).filter(Boolean);\n            if (!words.length) words = [\"Create\"];\n            var interval = num(vars.interval, 1.8, 0.8, 4);\n            var size = num(vars.font_size, 120, 24, 260);\n            var weight = [\"500\", \"600\", \"700\"].indexOf(String(vars.font_weight)) >= 0 ? String(vars.font_weight) : \"600\";\n            root.style.setProperty(\"--dt-color\", col(vars.color, \"#18181b\"));\n            [row, measure].forEach(function (e) { e.style.fontSize = size + \"px\"; e.style.fontWeight = weight; });\n            row.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", words.join(\", \"));\n\n            // Measure every word: where each character sits and how wide the word is.\n            function isDigit(c) { return c >= \"0\" && c <= \"9\"; }\n            function measureWord(w) {\n              measure.textContent = \"\";\n              var chars = Array.from(w);\n              chars.forEach(function (c) { var s = document.createElement(\"span\"); s.textContent = c; measure.appendChild(s); });\n              var toks = [];\n              chars.forEach(function (c, i) { if (c.trim() === \"\") return; toks.push({ char: c, x: measure.children[i].offsetLeft, digit: isDigit(c), slot: 0 }); });\n              var slot = 0;\n              for (var i = toks.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) if (toks[i].digit) toks[i].slot = slot++;\n              return { tokens: toks, width: measure.offsetWidth };\n            }\n            var meas = words.map(measureWord);\n            var widest = Math.max.apply(null, meas.map(function (m) { return m.width; }));\n            var avail = root.clientWidth * 0.9;\n            if (widest > avail) {\n              size = Math.max(24, size * avail / widest);\n              [row, measure].forEach(function (e) { e.style.fontSize = size + \"px\"; });\n              meas = words.map(measureWord);\n            }\n            var em = size;\n\n            // The physics, ported from the source's engine: springs for travel, lift, roll, squash, tilt and width.\n            var STEP = 1 / 120;\n            function damping(k, z) { return 2 * z * Math.sqrt(k); }\n            var TRAVEL_K = 140, TRAVEL_C = damping(140, 0.8), LIFT_K = 300, LIFT_C = damping(300, 0.9), ROLL_K = 200, ROLL_C = damping(200, 0.86);\n            var SQUASH_K = 1400, SQUASH_C = damping(1400, 0.6), TILT_K = 140, TILT_C = damping(140, 0.7), WIDTH_K = 220, WIDTH_C = damping(220, 1);\n            var GRAVITY = 32, DROP = 0.7, FALL_FADE = 0.9, ROLL = 0.75, LAND_SQUASH = -0.16, ENTER_STAGGER = 0.035, MAX_SPREAD = 0.45, FADE_RATE = 7;\n            var dur = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"7.2\");\n            var N = Math.ceil(dur / STEP) + 2;\n            var step = 0, glyphs = [], live = [], order = [], nextId = 0, w = meas[0].width, vw = 0, tw = w;\n            var Wd = new Float32Array(N);\n\n            function create(t) {\n              var g = { id: nextId++, char: t.char, digit: t.digit, slot: t.slot, phase: \"rest\", leaving: false, delay: 0, x: t.x, vx: 0, tx: t.x, x0: t.x, arc: 0, y: 0, vy: 0, ty: 0, r: 0, vr: 0, tr: 0, sq: 0, vsq: 0, o: 1,\n                X: new Float32Array(N), Y: new Float32Array(N), R: new Float32Array(N), Q: new Float32Array(N), O: new Float32Array(N) };\n              glyphs.push(g); live.push(g); return g;\n            }\n            function move(g, t) {\n              g.slot = t.slot; g.tx = t.x;\n              if (g.phase === \"rest\" && Math.abs(t.x - g.x) < 0.5) { g.x = t.x; return; }\n              g.x0 = g.x; g.delay = 0;\n              var distance = t.x - g.x;\n              g.arc = -Math.sign(distance) * Math.min(0.22 * em, Math.abs(distance) * 0.14);\n              g.phase = \"travel\";\n            }\n            function enter(g, dir, index) {\n              g.o = 0;\n              if (g.digit) { g.y = dir * ROLL * em; g.ty = 0; g.phase = \"roll\"; return; }\n              g.y = -DROP * em; g.phase = \"drop\"; g.delay = index * ENTER_STAGGER;\n            }\n            function leave(g, dir) {\n              g.leaving = true; g.delay = 0;\n              if (g.digit) { g.phase = \"roll\"; g.ty = -dir * ROLL * 1.2 * em; return; }\n              var side = g.x + em * 0.3 < tw / 2 ? -1 : 1;\n              g.tr = side * (5 + ((g.id * 7) % 11)); g.vx = side * 0.4 * em; g.vy = Math.max(g.vy, 0); g.phase = \"fall\";\n            }\n            function update(m) {\n              var tokens = m.tokens;\n              var letters = {}, slots = {};\n              order.forEach(function (g) { if (g.digit) slots[g.slot] = g; else (letters[g.char] = letters[g.char] || []).push(g); });\n              var before = Number(order.filter(function (g) { return g.digit; }).map(function (g) { return g.char; }).join(\"\"));\n              var after = Number(tokens.filter(function (t) { return t.digit; }).map(function (t) { return t.char; }).join(\"\"));\n              var dir = after < before ? -1 : 1;\n              var next = [], entering = 0;\n              tokens.forEach(function (t) {\n                var old;\n                if (t.digit) { old = slots[t.slot]; delete slots[t.slot]; }\n                else if (letters[t.char] && letters[t.char].length) old = letters[t.char].shift();\n                if (old && old.char === t.char) { move(old, t); next.push(old); return; }\n                if (old) leave(old, dir);\n                var g = create(t); enter(g, dir, entering++); next.push(g);\n              });\n              var spread = entering * ENTER_STAGGER;\n              if (spread > MAX_SPREAD) next.forEach(function (g) { g.delay *= MAX_SPREAD / spread; });\n              Object.keys(letters).forEach(function (k) { letters[k].forEach(function (g) { leave(g, dir); }); });\n              Object.keys(slots).forEach(function (k) { leave(slots[k], dir); });\n              order = next; tw = m.width;\n            }\n            function clamp01(x) { return x < 0 ? 0 : x > 1 ? 1 : x; }\n            function stepGlyph(g, h) {\n              if (g.phase === \"travel\") {\n                var span = Math.abs(g.tx - g.x0), p = span < 0.5 ? 1 : clamp01(1 - Math.abs(g.tx - g.x) / span);\n                g.ty = g.arc * 4 * p * (1 - p);\n                g.vx += (-TRAVEL_K * (g.x - g.tx) - TRAVEL_C * g.vx) * h; g.x += g.vx * h;\n                g.vy += (-LIFT_K * (g.y - g.ty) - LIFT_C * g.vy) * h; g.y += g.vy * h;\n                g.o = Math.min(1, g.o + FADE_RATE * h);\n              } else if (g.phase === \"drop\") {\n                g.vy += GRAVITY * em * h; g.y += g.vy * h;\n                if (g.y >= 0) { g.y = 0; g.vy = 0; g.sq = LAND_SQUASH; g.phase = \"rest\"; }\n                g.o = clamp01(1 + g.y / (DROP * em));\n              } else if (g.phase === \"fall\") {\n                g.vy += GRAVITY * em * h; g.y += g.vy * h; g.x += g.vx * h;\n                g.vr += (-TILT_K * (g.r - g.tr) - TILT_C * g.vr) * h; g.r += g.vr * h;\n                g.o = Math.min(g.o, clamp01(1 - g.y / (FALL_FADE * em)));\n              } else if (g.phase === \"roll\") {\n                g.vy += (-ROLL_K * (g.y - g.ty) - ROLL_C * g.vy) * h; g.y += g.vy * h;\n                g.o = clamp01(1 - Math.abs(g.y) / (ROLL * em));\n              }\n              if (g.sq !== 0 || g.vsq !== 0) {\n                g.vsq += (-SQUASH_K * g.sq - SQUASH_C * g.vsq) * h; g.sq += g.vsq * h;\n                if (Math.abs(g.sq) < 0.001 && Math.abs(g.vsq) < 0.01) { g.sq = 0; g.vsq = 0; }\n              }\n            }\n            function isGone(g) { return g.leaving && g.o <= 0.002; }\n            function settle(g) {\n              if (g.leaving) return;\n              var arrived = Math.abs(g.x - g.tx) < 0.05 && Math.abs(g.vx) < 0.5 && Math.abs(g.y) < 0.05 && Math.abs(g.vy) < 0.5;\n              if ((g.phase === \"travel\" && arrived) || (g.phase === \"roll\" && arrived)) { g.x = g.tx; g.y = 0; g.vx = 0; g.vy = 0; g.o = 1; g.phase = \"rest\"; }\n            }\n            var next = 0;\n            for (step = 0; step < N; step++) {\n              var t = step * STEP;\n              while (next < words.length && t >= next * interval - 1e-9) {\n                if (next === 0) { tw = meas[0].width; w = tw; }\n                update(meas[next]); next++;\n              }\n              live.forEach(function (g) {\n                if (g.delay > 0) { g.delay -= STEP; return; }\n                stepGlyph(g, STEP); settle(g);\n              });\n              if (Math.abs(w - tw) >= 0.1 || Math.abs(vw) >= 0.1) { vw += (-WIDTH_K * (w - tw) - WIDTH_C * vw) * STEP; w += vw * STEP; } else { w = tw; vw = 0; }\n              Wd[step] = w;\n              live.forEach(function (g) { g.X[step] = g.x; g.Y[step] = g.y; g.R[step] = g.r; g.Q[step] = g.sq; g.O[step] = g.o; });\n              live = live.filter(function (g) { return !isGone(g); });\n            }\n\n            // One element per glyph; the timeline reads the recorded simulation back.\n            glyphs.forEach(function (g) {\n              var el = document.createElement(\"span\");\n              el.className = \"dt-glyph\";\n              el.textContent = g.char;\n              row.appendChild(el);\n              g.el = el;\n            });\n            function draw(time) {\n              var f = Math.min(N - 2, Math.max(0, time / STEP)), i0 = Math.floor(f), u = f - i0;\n              function at(a) { return a[i0] + (a[i0 + 1] - a[i0]) * u; }\n              row.style.width = at(Wd).toFixed(2) + \"px\";\n              for (var i = 0; i < glyphs.length; i++) {\n                var g = glyphs[i], o = at(g.O);\n                if (o <= 0.002) { g.el.style.opacity = 0; continue; }\n                var sq = at(g.Q);\n                g.el.style.transform = \"translate(\" + at(g.X).toFixed(2) + \"px,\" + at(g.Y).toFixed(2) + \"px) rotate(\" + at(g.R).toFixed(2) + \"deg) scale(\" + (1 - sq * 0.6).toFixed(3) + \",\" + (1 + sq).toFixed(3) + \")\";\n                g.el.style.opacity = o.toFixed(3);\n              }\n            }\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            var clock = { t: 0 };\n            tl.to(clock, { t: dur, duration: dur, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(clock.t); } }, 0);\n            draw(0);\n\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"7.2\");\n            if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"dynamic-text\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
